  {
    "id": "moka-2",
    "summary": "future::Cache::and_compute_with removes its per-key waiter before writing to the cache, so a concurrent call on the same key reads the old value and one update is silently lost.",
    "location": [
      "src/future/value_initializer.rs:350",
      "src/future/value_initializer.rs:374"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "moka-5",
    "summary": "In sync::Cache, when expire_after_update returns None for an entry that has already expired, the expiration is not cleared, so the value just written stays unreadable.",
    "location": [
      "src/sync/base_cache.rs:689",
      "src/sync/base_cache.rs:696"
    ]
  }
